 "readings": {
  "R-ALG": "A wrong alg is malformed:alg. Table 3 lists cty, typ, row-type, family-id, edition and iss for malformed:<member> and does not name alg.",
  "R-DET-ORDER": "Step 1 checks determinism of the statement, then the protected header, then the payload, in the order Table 3 lists them.",
  "R-DIM-UNKNOWN": "B.1 shows an evidence row with a dimension but does not say the family requires one; dimension_missing is not decided for it (pass 1 inferred it did).",
  "R-IDTYPE-SET": "identity_type is a set (Section 6.2); one out of order is malformed:identity_type, since Table 3 names set_order only for sets in refs.",
  "R-KID-BY-SUB": "A held key record is found by the key its sub names; kid_mismatch is a record whose key member does not have the thumbprint its sub names.",
  "R-MAXSECS": "key_record_max_secs is not in the draft; the upper bound of the end rule is not checked.",
  "R-MISSING-MEMBER": "A protected-header member that is missing is malformed:<member>; a member that should not be there is unexpected:protected.",
  "R-MIXED-FIRST": "key_record_mixed_roles is checked before key_record_out_of_window. Table 3 lists them the other way, but a mixed set always breaks the end rule, so in that order the mixed reason could never be given.",
  "R-RAW-WAIT": "A verifier holding bare keys only (directory raw) cannot show ways 2 to 4 of Section 6.2; kid other than the thumbprint in iss is Waiting on the key record those ways need.",
  "R-REGISTRY": "Whether a family or a dimension is registered is in [CC], not in the draft. A family the draft names is taken as registered; any other leaves the answer conditional.",
  "R-ROTATION": "A rotation record names its predecessor's record in refs.prev or refs.target and is carried by a statement of the predecessor key over the same payload. Section 6.2 does not say which member; pass 1 read prev only.",
  "R-ROWTYPE": "A row type that is a text string outside the five passes verification and is refused at admission with attestation_type_unregistered (Section 3, Table 4); a non-text value is malformed:row-type.",
  "R-SET-OUTSIDE-REFS": "An array member the draft does not define is a set (Section 4.3); one out of order is set_order:<member>. Section 4.3 names federation_set_semantics_unsorted, which Tables 3 and 4, said to be the complete list, do not carry.",
  "R-STEP9-AUTHOR": "Where the draft does not say whether a family is authored, an author member present is read as authored and iss must equal it; roles are not known.",
  "R-VU-GENERAL": "valid_until_not_after_asserted_at applies to every row (Table 3, step 4), though the CDDL comment states it for accord rows."
 }
